  "caveats": [
    "Measurement, not a proof: seeded Monte Carlo against a curveball (fixed-margin) null, per house rules.",
    "j=2,3 (tilt) and j=5 (oblique astigmatism) are structurally zero for ANY matrix under this pipeline: PCA scores are mean-centred (kills the m=1 tilt moments) and PC1/PC2 are uncorrelated by construction (kills mean(u*v), i.e. the sin(2theta) moment). Their nulls are degenerate, so they are inadmissible by construction rather than by evidence.",
    "Share coordinates are compositional (they sum to 1 over j>=2), so the 14 z-scores are not independent tests and no multiplicity correction is applied.",
    "Several null share distributions are extremely tight (sd ~1e-4), so the corresponding z magnitudes are very large and hypersensitive to the repo's documented over-dispersion of finite-MC z. Treat the magnitudes as ordinal, not calibrated.",
    "Disk radial order n and sphere degree l are different quantum numbers; the by-n vs by-l table is a lift-footprint diagnostic, not an identification.",
    "The disk side excludes piston (a_1 = 1 identically); the sphere side is quoted both raw and renormalized over l=1..3 for a like-for-like read."
  ]
